Subject: [PATCH] xpm: drop RAM_DECOMP so bram_dp_xpm builds on Vivado 2022.1

QICK targets Vivado 2023.1 (see firmware/projects/*/bd_2023-1.tcl). The E200
flow is pinned to 2022.1 because PetaLinux 2022.1 builds linux-xlnx 5.15.19,
which is what the ADI kernel patch in antsdr-pynq matches.

bram_dp_xpm.sv passes RAM_DECOMP to xpm_memory_tdpram, and that parameter does
not exist in the 2022.1 XPM library:

    ERROR: [Synth 8-7136] In the module 'xpm_memory_tdpram' declared at
    '.../xpm_memory.sv:8964', parameter 'RAM_DECOMP' used as named parameter
    override, does not exist

"auto" is RAM_DECOMP's own default, so dropping the override is functionally
neutral. Verified by synthesising axis_signal_gen_v6 (N_DDS=1, N=12) for
xc7z020clg484-1: 0 errors, 0 critical warnings.

There is exactly one such override in the file (line 428); the other textual
match for RAM_DECOMP is the parameter-documentation comment block.
---
diff --git a/firmware/hdl/bram_dp_xpm.sv b/firmware/hdl/bram_dp_xpm.sv
--- a/firmware/hdl/bram_dp_xpm.sv
+++ b/firmware/hdl/bram_dp_xpm.sv
@@ -425,7 +425,6 @@ module bram_dp_xpm #(
       .MEMORY_PRIMITIVE                ("auto"),               // String
       .MEMORY_SIZE                     (B*2**N),               // DECIMAL
       .MESSAGE_CONTROL                 (0),                    // DECIMAL
-      .RAM_DECOMP                      ("auto"),               // String
       .READ_DATA_WIDTH_A               (B),                    // DECIMAL
       .READ_DATA_WIDTH_B               (B),                    // DECIMAL
       .READ_LATENCY_A                  (1+OUT_REG_ENA),        // DECIMAL
